    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0341" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1154.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-14T16:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 11, 11 a.m. The Receivership has been instructed to advance $3,500 per
                    diem instead of the $2,000 already arranged for. This sum will be advanced for a
                    period of fifteen days. It is expected from your reports that a longer campaign
                    will not be necessary. Unless Congress approves proposition for loan before
                    period of fifteen days is passed all available funds will be exhausted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
